# The same overlap, made safe the way WORKPLAN.md says to make it safe: one
# task depends on the other, so they are never claimable at the same time and
# there is nothing to collide. This is the shape the rule allows, and a check
# that refused every overlap it saw would refuse it too.
run available
exit 0
file tasks/M1-01.md
	---
	id: M1-01
	owns:
	  - crates/normalize
	depends_on: []
	exclusive: no
	---
file tasks/M1-02.md
	---
	id: M1-02
	owns:
	  - crates/normalize
	depends_on: [M1-01]
	exclusive: no
	---
stdout
	M1-01
